@startuml
title Step 9+ (Network slice related service & resource order items) - NSMF Responsibility

participant "Service Order\nManagement" as SOM #blue
participant "Service Catalog\nManagement" as SCM #blue
participant "Service Inventory" as SI #blue

note over SOM : Receives Service order\nfor Network Slice RFS with\nService Profile reference

== NSMF Responsibility ==

SOM -> SOM : 1 Decompose Network Slice Order

note over SOM : Derive Service Profile parameters\nand Network slice specific\nrequirements

SOM -> SI : 2 **TMF638 Service Inventory Management**\nPOST /service\n(state="active")
activate SI
SI --> SOM : 3 **TMF638** 200 RFS (Service Profile)
deactivate SI

SOM -> SCM : 4 **TMF633 Service Catalog Management**\nGET /resourceSpecification
activate SCM
SCM --> SOM : 5 **TMF633** 200 Network Slice RFS Specifications, Service Profile RFS Specification
deactivate SCM

note over SOM : Get all the Network slice instances\nmatching the Service Profile

SOM -> SI : 6 **TMF638 Service Inventory Management**\nGET /service\nfilter by Service Profile association, state="active"
activate SI
SI --> SOM : 7 **TMF638** 201 RFS (Network Slice RFS Instance)
deactivate SI

SOM -> SCM : 8 **TMF633 Service Catalog Management**\nGET /resourceSpecification
activate SCM
SCM --> SOM : 9 **TMF633** 200 Network Slice Subnet RFS Specifications, Slice Subnet Profile RFS Specification
deactivate SCM

note over SOM : Derive Slice Profile parameters and\nSlice Subnet related requirements

SOM -> SI : 10 **TMF638 Service Inventory Management**\nPOST /service\n(state="active")
activate SI
SI --> SOM : 11 **TMF638** 200 RFS (Slice Profile)
deactivate SI

note over SOM : Check RFS alternatives

note over SOM : Carry out qualitative and quantitative design.\nQualitative & Quantitative design based on Service Profile parameters

SOM -> SI : 12 **TMF638 Service Inventory Management**\nPATCH /service\n(state="designed")
activate SI
SI --> SOM : 13 **TMF638** 201 RFS
deactivate SI

alt If New Slice Instance Required

    opt for each NSS associated with NSI
        note over SOM : **AllocateNSSI** on NSSMF
        SOM -> SOM : 14 <<3GPP>>AllocateNSSI
    end

else If Existing Slice is Reused

    opt If Modification of NSI parameters required
        SOM -> SOM : 15 <<3GPP>>ModifyNSI Operation

        SOM -> SI : 16 **TMF638 Service Inventory Management**\nPATCH /service\n(state="designed")
        activate SI
        SI --> SOM : 17 **TMF638** 201 RFS
        deactivate SI
    end

    opt for each NSS associated with NSI
        note over SOM : **modifyNSSI** on NSSMF
        SOM -> SOM : 18 <<3GPP>>ModifyNSSI Operation
    end

end

@enduml
